   "concept": {
    "name": "Brick Tide Jetty",
    "tagline": "Square waves, round breath.",
    "brief": "You sit on the last wide brick at the end of the jetty with your feet over the teal water, and the simple stepped shapes around you give your eyes somewhere clean and orderly to rest. Breathe in for the slow swell and out for the gentle slap against the bricks, and let each thought settle onto a stud like something you can set down and leave there.",
    "image_prompt": "Wide eye-level photograph of a sunlit tropical cove at golden hour, with the sand falling away in neat square-cut terraces to calm teal water. A jetty of oversized sand-coloured, teal and white interlocking bricks with round studs on top runs out into the shallows. Warm low sun casts long crisp shadows, palms with flat blocky fronds lean in from the edge, and a single neon lime brick glows at the jetty's end. Wet sand shines, the sea is glassy with small ripples, and the sky fades from pale gold to deep blue.",
